n  that moment  bruce wayne truly becomes batman  brian singer's superman returns was  intended to be a continuation of  christopher reeve's superman films but  was criticized for its somber depiction  of the man of steel  and the unnecessary introduction of  superman's son  jason nevertheless superman returns is  filled with plenty of visually stunning  sequences  in which superman shows off his godlike  abilities one particularly memorable  scene occurs shortly after superman's  return when he floats above the earth  and uses his super hearing to listen to  all the voices on the planet  as soon as he hears a single cry for  help he leaps into action and plummets  back down to earth  whatever his flaws may be superman is  supposed to be earth's greatest  protector  and this scene demonstrates that in full  heath ledger's magnetic performance as  the joker in the dark knight earned him  a well-deserved posthumous oscar  and while virtually all of ledger scenes  could be considered iconic in their  own right the interrogation scene  between batman and the joker is probably  the best of all  in this scene the joker takes the  opportunity offered by his face to face  with batman  to deliver some of the best lines in  comic book movie history  see i'm not a monster  i'm just ahead of the curve this is a  truly gripping scene  made even more disturbing by the fact  that the joker makes  no effort to defend himself when things  get violent yet still manages to get  everything he wants as far as depictions  of the joker go  it really doesn't get much better than  this  while there are a few slight differences  between zack snyder's watchmen  adaptation and the comic on which it's  based one iconic scene is especially  faithful to the original work  the birth of dr manhattan being the only  character in the story with  actual superpowers dr manhattan's  creation is suitably dramatic  after being accidentally locked in a  test chamber scientist john ostermann is  literally  