nally locked  into his crusade  christopher nolan's dark knight trilogy  offers something new closure  here and nowhere else bruce wayne is  finally able to enjoy the happy ending  he deserves  zack snyder's man of steel is full of  controversial choices  from the movie's grim tone to superman's  decision to kill  general zod at the story's climax this  film continues to divide fans to this  day  one scene however truly embraces the joy  of being superman  upon discovering a kryptonian scout ship  in the arctic clark kent  dons his kryptonian suit and steps into  the sun ready to learn how to fly  gradually clark progresses from super  leaps to actual flight  soaring through clouds and canyons  before finally reaching orbit  the look on superman's face as he  realizes what he can be is genuinely  heartwarming and  demonstrates the true potential of  superman at his best  batman vs superman attracted all kinds  of criticism when it was released in  2016 but one thing the movie did get  right was the titular showdown between  the man of steel and the dark knight  tell me  do you plead this sequence sees an older  deadlier bruce wayne employ  everything from sonic cannons to  kryptonite gas to gain the edge on his  god-like opponent  and it works too although the two  eventually stop fighting to team up  batman definitely gets in a good few  hits against superman and  at one point almost takes him down for  good it's a potent reminder of just how  powerful  a well-prepared batman can be while  suicide squad received countless dire  reviews from the critics  many of them at least praised both the  action and margot robbie's performance  as harley quinn however  it's another character will smith's  deadshot who stars in the movie's most  iconic scene  when his team ends up fighting an army  of demonic monsters the master assassin  deadshot manages to convince the  villains to fight alongside the military  to survive  then just as the demons threaten to  overwhelm them deadshot  steps up he uses his uncanny aim and an  arsenal of weaponry to take out  every single demon even as they get  close enough to tear him apart  by the end of the film deadshot is still  anything but a hero  but he has still managed to earn the  respect of even his hard-nosed military  handler  wonder woman's best scene perfectly  communicates exactly who wonder woman  is and where her strengths lie as a hero  after accompanying steve trevor to  europe to help fight world war  1 diana finds herself on the front lines  in belgium  here steve claims that moving through  the battlefield is more or less  impossible as the men have been fighting  for months and barely gained an inch of  ground in that time  in response diana removes her cloak  climbs the parapet and begins to walk  across  no man's land a barrage of bullets and  bombs try to bring her down but the  amazonian princess refuses to give up  eventually leading the allied forces to  victory it's a stunningly shot action  sequence  that really shows wonder woman for the  inspirational symbol of strength that  she is  the theatrical release of justice league  greatly altered zack snyder's original  vision  as such it's also deeply unpopular among  the fans who successfully lobbied for  the release of zack snyder's justice  league in march 2021.  one scene however did excite many fans  back in 2017  after being resurrected by an alien  mother box superman emerges from his  tomb in an amnesiac state  and almost immediately attacks the newly  formed justice league  their combined might isn't nearly enough  to restrain him  of course and he even proves himself  fast enough to keep  up with the flash himself obviously  superman later returns as the justice  league's ally but this scene did a  pretty great job in showing why you  don't mess with the last son of krypton  fully embracing the fantastical aspects  of the character  aquaman immerses its hero in an atlantis  bursting with color and life  there he accepts a quest to recover a  powerful trident that will grant him  control over all  sea life what this really means is made  clear in the movie's climactic battle  scene in which aquaman shows up to an  all-out war  between opposing undersea kingdoms  drawing on his enhanced powers  aquaman summons an army of sharks whales  and sea monsters that utterly overwhelms  his opponents  it might sound like a silly power on  paper but aquaman  showed for the first time on screen that  arthur curry's powers  really are no joke at the heart of  shazam is  every kid's wish to become an  all-powerful superhero  the first half of the film takes a  comedic approach to this premise as  fourteen-year-old billy batson gains the  ability to transform into a fully adult  superhero  hey to fighting bad guys  you that is an actual vomit however the  film's best scene comes at the climax  when billy stumbles onto a unique  solution to stop the evil dr savannah  and his seven deadly sins  sharing his power with his foster  siblings as the kids  all shout shazam a bolt of lightning  transforms them into fully grown  superheroes  ready to take on savannah's army while  comic book fans might already be  familiar with the shazam family  this scene will doubtless surprise and  delight all kinds of fans in equal  measure  joker is a movie that managed to do what  no other  dc film does turn the clown prince of  crime into a genuinely sympathetic  character  the constant abuse levied against failed  comedian arthur fleck comes to a head  when he's invited onto a late night talk  show hosted by murray franklin the man  he once idolized  having previously been pushed to the  edge by murray's ridicule arthur  now fully inhabiting the joker persona  decides to take his revenge  originally planning to shoot himself on  live television arthur changes his mind  at the last second  and shoots murray in the face instead no  longer an insecure sad sack  this is a joker who has fully embraced  his demons showing how the most  human super villains could be the very  worst of all  margot robbie reprised her role as the  joker's ex-girlfriend harley quinn in  birds of prey and the result is an  off-the-wall film filled with delirious  fun the full title of the movie speaks  to the film's broader aims while  it's best scene perfectly communicates  them it's all about helping harley and  the birds find themselves  after being dumped by the joker harley  decides to reinvent herself by blowing  up ace chemicals  the factory where the joker transformed  her into his chalk white's counterpart  although harley makes this decision when  she's drunk and feeling impulsive  it's still a fantastic moment of rebirth  that decisively separates harley from  the joker's influence  as the factory goes up in an explosion  of flaming green smoke  and charlotte lawrence's the jokes on  you plays in the background  all of gotham city learns that harley  quinn is finally her own woman  wonder woman 1984 shows off a more  vulnerable side to diana  one who accidentally wishes for her dead  lover steve trevor to return to her  her wish comes true but as a consequence  diana's power begins to fade  this becomes a problem when she and  steve travel to egypt where the film's  antagonist  maxwell lord has taken control of an oil  tycoon's personal army  as wonder woman takes on the entire  convoy she discovers to reduce  strength speed and stamina make the  battle much harder  it's a very different side to wonder  woman especially compared to the one we  saw storming no man's land in the first  movie  despite it all she refuses to back down  and that's what makes the scene  so memorable one thing that most people  agree on about  zack snyder's vision of the dc eu is  that it's all  pretty dark this is made abundantly  clear in zack snyder's justice league  and arguably the film's most iconic  scene is the most despondent of all  for its epilogue the movie returns to  the apocalyptic  nightmare future